  "depends_on": [],
  "summary": "The channel function table (gk110_chan) describes per-channel resources: an instance block (inst) that holds PBDMA state, a USERD area (userd) containing the command-buffer put/get pointers visible to the GPU driver, and a RAMFC block (ramfc) that the PBDMA reads to fetch commands. The table provides bind/unbind to attach or detach a channel, start/stop to enable or disable it, and preempt for GPU preemption. On channel bind the driver writes the instance-block address and runlist ID to channel control registers (0x800000\u20130x800004), then writes a full set of RAMFC state values (command-buffer base address, size, USERD address, privilege flag, channel ID) into the instance block before calling nvkm_done to commit the changes."
}
